Intends to alleviate the financial burden of informal sector workers, self-employed individuals, peddlers, contractual workers, and other workers under a \"no work, no pay\" arrangement who are greatly affected during the occurrence of COVID-19 global pandemic since they are not assured of any income during the quarantine period.
Proposes to have a 30-day waiver of payments to the following:
a) loan amortizations and premium contributions to SSS, GSIS, Pag-IBIG Fund, and PhilHealth;
b) rental payments for dwelling units and commercial spaces in private establishments;
c) subscription payments with internet service providers and telecommunication companies;
d) toll fees for use of expressways; and
e) public utilities such as electric and water consumption.

Aims to establish an epidemic/pandemic emergency plan in order for the country to be better prepared to recognize and manage future threats of epidemic/pandemic.
Proposes for an intensive nationwide information campaign on emerging/re-emerging infectious diseases to educate the people on its nature, causes, transmission and prevention.
Proposes the establishment of Endemic/Pandemic Emergency Council which shall: 
a) Identify isolation centers and health care facilities; 
b) Authorize quarantine of individuals or groups of individuals;
c) Purchase, store or distribute sufficiently adequate supply of PPEs, anti-viral agents, anti-toxins, serums and vaccines, and ensure that their use and rationing be controlled, restricted and regulated in the event of an epidemic/pandemic;
d) Establish a comprehensive monitoring program to determine the sufficiency and effectiveness of the programs and activities in preventing the spread of the disease;
e) Establish reporting procedures that will ensure the confidentiality and non-disclosure of the personal information gathered and medical records of all patients and individuals infected or suspected to have been infected with the disease;
f) Provide health care workers and responders with adequate PPEs like N95 respiratory masks, gloves, face shields and goggles.

Seeks to create a National Health Strategy that would provide for an integrated policy coordination and
strategic direction with respect to all matters in relation to the national public health and medical preparedness as well as execution and deployment of national response before, during, and immediately after public health emergencies.
Defines Public Health Emergency as an occurrence of imminent threat of an illness or condition caused by bioterrorism, epidemic or pandemic disease, or a novel and highly fatal infectious agent or biological toxin, that poses a substantial risk of a significant number of human facilities or incidents or permanent or long-term disability.
Proposes among others the following provisions:
a) a review of health strategies every five (5) years, or more frequently as deemed necessary;
b) creation of an Inter-Agency Task Force on public health emergencies composed of representatives 
  from: DOH, DILG, NDRRMC, DFA, DPWH, DOTr and NEDA;
c) components of a National Health Strategy which shall be consistent with international health         regulations;
d) creation of medical reserve corps composed of volunteer health professionals

Provides that the PNIDHRC shall be the principal hospital and research facility responsible for the: 
a.	treatment, control, prevention, and research of highly communicable diseases whether from natural or man-made sources; 
b.	conduct researches and advocate government actions and policies to solve medical health problems; 
c.	seek to improve the management of infectious diseases including ill-effects to the health of humans of various hazardous chemical; 
d.	conduct surveillance and clinical researches on important pathogens; and
e.	perform molecular epidemiology to investigate the mechanisms contributing the drug resistant pathogens.                   
Proposes to appropriate the sum of Twenty Billion Pesos for the initial operation and maintenance of the hospitals and research facilities of the PNIDHRC and thereafter, the necessary amount to support its continued operation and maintenance shall be appropriated in the GAA.
